{"questions":[{"question_id":"1ky3zv2p9","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2014 Paper 1 Offline","year":2014,"examDate":2014,"subject":"physics","chapter":"heat-and-thermodynamics","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"heat-engine-second-law-of-thermodynamics-and-carnot-engine","type":"integer","marks":3,"negMarks":0,"permalink":"a-thermodynamic-system-is-taken-from-an-initial-state-i-with-jee-advanced-physics-units-and-measurements-wewn7qtv2f2utpzc","content":"A thermodynamic system is taken from an initial state i with internal energy U<sub>i</sub> = 100 J to the final state f along two different paths iaf and ibf, as schematically shown in the figure. The work done by the system along the paths af, ib and bf are W<sub>af</sub> = 200 J, W<sub>ib</sub> = 50 J and W<sub>bf</sub> = 100 J respectively. The heat supplied to the system along the path iaf, ib and bf are Q<sub>iaf</sub>, Q<sub>ib</sub> and Q<sub>bf</sub> respectively. If the internal energy of the system in the state b is U<sub>b</sub> = 200 J and Q<sub>iaf</sub> = 500 J, the ratio Q<sub>bf</sub> / Q<sub>ib</sub> is <br><br> <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1ky4ipydq/9ffb827e-062c-4a4f-bbeb-7fb69634b4ec/87e8e6e0-6fc9-11ec-8887-d75613c1bf3a/file-1ky4ipydr.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1ky4ipydq/9ffb827e-062c-4a4f-bbeb-7fb69634b4ec/87e8e6e0-6fc9-11ec-8887-d75613c1bf3a/file-1ky4ipydr.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;max-height: 60vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2014 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Heat and Thermodynamics Question 42 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1ky4ipydq/9ffb827e-062c-4a4f-bbeb-7fb69634b4ec/87e8e6e0-6fc9-11ec-8887-d75613c1bf3a/file-1ky4ipydr.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1ky4ipydq/9ffb827e-062c-4a4f-bbeb-7fb69634b4ec/87e8e6e0-6fc9-11ec-8887-d75613c1bf3a/file-1ky4ipydr.png?format=png 750w, https://app-cont